{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448357-a-storyteller-s-guide-to-creating-changing-breeds","id":1448357,"title":"a Storyteller's Guide to Creating Changing Breeds?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-12T14:00:41-07:00","id":1448357,"title":"a Storyteller's Guide to Creating Changing Breeds?","content":"Basically I'm working on a project that involves a large number of home brew Fera, and it got me thinking about trying to create a guide to enable other storytellers to custom make their own changing breeds, but I'm unsure what sort of framework to create, I checked the Infamous CoD Changing Breeds Book, as it has a guide like this that potentially could serve as a starting point but I'm not sure how to reverse engineer such a thing, as its built for a different system. <br /> <br /> I want to know what are they keys to creating a well balanced fera, the CoD Book suggests against making a T-Rex, which is already useless advice with the Mokole here, so setting balance must also be a factor as WtF is a much smaller scope setting then WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T15:03:04-07:00","id":1448359,"title":"","content":"The first thing to consider is that each Changing Breed was made to serve a purpose under Gaia, or another powerful creator, such as the Weaver. The main thrust of the breed should not duplicate directly what has already been done, unless you want the breed to belong to the Triat or another such being. Next, think about the animal half in question. Some animals already have analogs in myth and folklore that would easily accommodate a Changing Breed; others do not. Consider the systems and rules already in place and see what can be adapted and what could be ignored. For instance, is the Breed lunar or solar aspected? To they have Rage? How many forms do they have and what stats change with each form? Should there be Auspices or Tribes? Which Gifts and Rites can be shared/transferred? Should the Breed be believed lost or extinct, or is it brand new? What is the geographical range? How does the Breed interact with the Umbra, if at all? I've been thinking a book of lost and new Tribes/Changing Breeds, including systems for creating them, would be a great idea. For the last little bit, I've been thinking about a new Breed being formed to represent Gaia's hope for a better tomorrow, but I really don't have the abilities/time to create such a work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T15:52:34-07:00","id":1448363,"title":"","content":"I thought that new breed was already in the lore as the Kitsune, but I get your point, I figures there are two or three major points where overlap of purpose is acceptable, the Age of Kings, the Lead up to the insect wars, and the Sea.<br /> <br /> the time of the dinosaur Kings is a bit nebulous, as shattered dreams indicates the first breeds were made in the Triassic and didn't strictly have a purpose, indicating that their assigned tasks were given later.<br /> <br /> the Time of the insect breeds occupies an unsure time, many assume it should be pre-Dinosaur, but the kinds of insects that the weaver would uplift into a changing breed would not live until the mid Jurassic, that said in the time immediately following the Wonder Work of the Wyrm, it would be a perfect opening for the weaver to try and fill the Niche, these could even be the very first breeds specifically created with assigned purposes built into their being, before they all got destroyed by the Ananasi and then supplanted by the rise of mammals<br /> <br /> the Sea is the best place to have overlap of purpose with land breeds, messengers, spies, builders, Jailers.<br /> <br /> One book that really inspired me was Tribe Book Mockeries, a cheap one that among its offerings, offered an alternative take where all the Mockery breeds were corrupted revivals of lost breeds.<br /> <br /> there are also Breeds mentioned in the lore but never named or given stats, and I'm left wondering what they could be and what their purpose was.<br /> those breeds being<br /> an unnamed ammonite breed said to be at war with the Rokea (could expand into a whole cephelapod breed and connect to the Octopus parasites from book of the wyrm)<br /> a Primative mammal breed describes as a &quot;Bristlecreeper&quot; that did not survive the wonderwork or otherwise died off before homonids developed<br /> Were-Megatheriums said to have been casualties of the war of Rage<br /> some manner of fresh water fish changing breed (possibly a reference to an April fools magazine about were-bass)<br /> Were otters<br /> and a couple of different bird of prey shifters that I assume were probably all the same Fera same as the bastet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}